# BYN1072: early exit in a block

A style lint (`guards.postfix`): reported by `bayan check` only, never by `build`, `run` or `test`. Its severity comes from `lints` in `package.byn` (`.suggestion` by default; `.none` silences it, `.error` makes `bayan check` fail).

**What.** An `if` without `else` or `unless`/`unlikely`/`never` whose block holds only one `return`, `fail`, `break` or `continue`.

**Why.** A postfix guard says the same on one line and keeps the exit at the left margin (spec §7.3, [style guide](../bayan-style.md)).

**Example.**

```
if cart.lines.isEmpty {
    fail .emptyCart
}
```

**Fix.** Write the exit with a postfix guard (the fix does it when the block holds the one statement and no comment):

```
fail .emptyCart if cart.lines.isEmpty
```
